From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: ggml-cpu: run the fused attention op on the CPU

GGML_OP_FUSED_ATTN (ggml_fused_relpos_attn, ggml_fused_attn_cached) had a
CUDA kernel only, so graphs built on it could not run on the CPU backend
and the MagpieTTS slot-arena decoder (one circular K/V cache row per
in-flight request, indexed by slot_ids) had no CPU path or CPU reference.
Add a reference CPU forward with the CUDA semantics: per-batch-item slot,
ring head and optional valid length, per-item mask columns, the
relative-position rel-shift, F32/F16 K/V/P, and the chunk appended to the
circular cache at ring_head after every thread has read it.

Callers that pick the fused op by backend (FastConformer, MagpieTTS) still
gate it on CUDA, so their CPU graphs are unchanged.

Upstream: stays here with the op it implements.

